# 🚀 Prosno.io — 10 Feature Improvement Ideas for UX

> **Perspective**: Senior Product Engineer | **Date**: March 14, 2026  
> Based on a deep audit of the current codebase: models, routes, templates, utilities, and existing feature set.

---

## 1. 🎯 Smart Question Paper Builder (Drag & Drop)

**Problem**: The current generation flow is linear — pick class → subject → chapters → generate. Users can't visually curate or reorder questions before generating.

**Proposed UX**:
- Add a **drag-and-drop paper builder** where teachers can:
  - Browse questions from the bank and drag them into a "paper canvas"
  - Reorder questions visually, group by section (MCQ / SQ / CQ)
  - Set per-section marks and time allocations
  - Preview the final paper layout in real-time before export
- Support **mixed-chapter papers** with visual chapter tags on each question

**Impact**: Transforms paper creation from "slot machine randomizer" to a **professional authoring tool**. Teachers get full creative control.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| High | Very High | ⭐ P0 |

---

## 2. 📊 Student Performance Analytics Dashboard

**Problem**: After a quiz ends, teachers see basic scores. There's no longitudinal view of student performance or question-level analytics.

**Proposed UX**:
- **For Teachers**: A dashboard showing:
  - Per-question accuracy rates (which questions were hardest?)
  - Time-spent-per-question heatmap
  - Student performance trends across multiple quizzes
  - Class average vs. individual student comparisons
  - Export analytics as PDF reports for parent-teacher meetings
- **For Students** (future): A personal progress tracker showing strengths and weak chapters

**Impact**: Turns Prosno from a **generation tool** into a **learning analytics platform**. Massive differentiation.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| Medium | Very High | ⭐ P0 |

---

## 3. 🔄 Collaborative Paper Creation (Multi-Teacher)

**Problem**: Currently, paper generation is single-user. In real schools, multiple teachers often collaborate on exam papers (e.g., subject coordinator + class teacher).

**Proposed UX**:
- Allow a teacher to **invite collaborators** to a question set via email/link
- Collaborators can add/remove/reorder questions
- Real-time presence indicators ("Rahim is editing...")
- **Approval workflow**: One teacher suggests questions, the senior teacher approves
- Version history showing who added which question

**Impact**: Matches how exam papers are actually created in schools. Strong differentiator for institutional adoption.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| High | High | P1 |

---

## 4. 📱 Progressive Web App (PWA) with Offline Mode

**Problem**: Many teachers in Bangladesh have unreliable internet. The app is fully server-rendered with no offline capability.

**Proposed UX**:
- Convert to a **PWA** with:
  - Offline access to previously generated papers and saved question sets
  - Background sync — create papers offline, upload when back online
  - Push notifications for bank question approvals, quiz results, badge awards
  - "Install to Home Screen" prompt for mobile users
- Cache the teacher's library and recent papers in IndexedDB

**Impact**: Critical for the Bangladesh market. Teachers can prepare papers at home without internet and sync at school.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| High | Very High | ⭐ P0 |

---

## 5. 🤖 AI-Powered Question Enhancement & Difficulty Calibration

**Problem**: The AI generator ([ai_generator.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/utils/ai_generator.py)) creates questions, but there's no way to refine, improve, or calibrate difficulty of existing questions — whether human-written or AI-generated.

**Proposed UX**:
- **"Enhance with AI" button** on any question:
  - Suggests better distractors for MCQs (common misconception-based options)
  - Rewrites unclear question stems for better readability
  - Translates between English ↔ Bengali with educational context preserved
- **Difficulty auto-calibration**:
  - After quizzes, use actual student performance data to auto-tag question difficulty
  - "85% of students got this right → Easy" vs. "Only 12% → Hard"
- **Similar question generator**: "Generate 5 variations of this question"

**Impact**: Bridges the gap between AI and human authoring. Makes every teacher's questions better.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| Medium | High | P1 |

---

## 6. 🎮 Interactive Quiz Modes (Beyond MCQ)

**Problem**: The quiz system ([quiz.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/routes/quiz.py)) only supports MCQ-style questions. Short Questions and Creative Questions have no interactive quiz format.

**Proposed UX**:
- **Timed Short Answer mode**: Students type answers, AI evaluates with partial credit
- **CQ Structured Response mode**: Multi-part question with expandable text fields for (ক), (খ), (গ), (ঘ) parts
- **"Rapid Fire" mode**: Fast-paced MCQ with 10-second timers and combo scoring
- **Team Quiz mode**: Split the class into teams, questions assigned round-robin
- **Practice mode**: Students can take self-paced quizzes without a teacher present, with instant explanations

**Impact**: Makes the quiz feature viable for more question types and learning scenarios. Huge engagement boost.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| High | High | P1 |

---

## 7. 📋 Question Paper Templates & Institutional Branding

**Problem**: Generated papers use a single fixed layout. Schools want their logo, specific formatting, custom headers/footers, and board-specific templates.

**Proposed UX**:
- **Template gallery**: Pre-built templates for SSC, HSC, JSC, PSC board exam formats
- **Custom branding**: Upload school logo, set institution name, add signatures
- **Layout customization**:
  - Choose between single/double column
  - Configure answer sheet format (OMR bubble vs. written)
  - Set custom headers, footers, watermarks
- **Save as institutional template** for reuse across the school

**Impact**: Makes papers look professional and school-specific. Key feature for institutional sales.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| Medium | High | P1 |

---

## 8. 🔔 Smart Notification & Activity Feed System

**Problem**: The notification system ([bank_notifications.html](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/templates/main/bank_notifications.html)) exists but is basic. Teachers miss important events and there's no engagement loop.

**Proposed UX**:
- **Rich activity feed** with categories:
  - 🏆 "Your question was used in 15 papers this week!"
  - ⭐ "Teacher Karim rated your Physics MCQ 5 stars"
  - 📝 "3 new questions added to your favorite chapter"
  - 🎖️ "You earned the 'Top Contributor' badge!"
- **Digest emails**: Weekly summary of your impact (questions used, ratings received)
- **Follow a teacher**: Get notified when they publish new questions
- **Follow a chapter/subject**: Get notified when new quality questions are added

**Impact**: Creates a **social engagement loop** that drives repeat usage and content contribution.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| Medium | Medium | P2 |

---

## 9. 🔍 Advanced Search with Filters & Question Preview

**Problem**: The search ([search.py](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/utils/search.py) + Meilisearch) is functional but basic. No way to preview questions before adding them to a paper.

**Proposed UX**:
- **Advanced filter panel**:
  - Filter by: difficulty, question type, board year, marks, rating, teacher reputation
  - "Board exam frequency" tag: "This topic appeared in SSC 2023, 2024"
  - Sort by: most used, highest rated, newest, most bookmarked
- **Inline question preview**: Hover/click to see the full question with answer without navigating away
- **"Add to Paper" one-click action** from search results
- **Search history & saved searches**: "Show me all Hard CQs for Physics Chapter 3"
- **Visual question cards** with metadata badges (difficulty pill, rating stars, usage count)

**Impact**: Makes discovering quality questions effortless. Reduces time-to-paper from minutes to seconds.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| Medium | High | P1 |

---

## 10. 🌐 Student Self-Study Portal

**Problem**: Currently, students only interact via live quizzes. There's no self-paced study experience.

**Proposed UX**:
- **Chapter-wise practice**: Students select a chapter and get unlimited practice questions
- **Spaced repetition**: System resurfaces questions the student got wrong after 1, 3, 7 days
- **Progress tracking**: Visual chapter completion map ("You've mastered 70% of Chapter 4")
- **Explained answers**: After answering, show the correct answer with a brief explanation (AI-generated or teacher-written)
- **Weak area recommendations**: "You struggle with Optics. Here are 10 targeted questions."
- **Peer comparison** (optional): "You're in the top 20% for this chapter"

**Impact**: Transforms Prosno from a **teacher tool** to a **teacher + student platform**. Doubles the addressable market.

| Effort | Value | Priority |
|--------|-------|----------|
| Very High | Very High | ⭐ P0 |

